 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Underlying exposure limit
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or margined in, the same underlying currency - for example several BTC-margined futures, or several coins quoted in the same stablecoin - a move in that underlying currency can hit multiple open positions at once. `max_underlying_exposure` limits the combined stake committed to open trades sharing the same underlying currency to a configurable share of total tradable capital.
+
+The "underlying currency" of a pair is its settlement currency where the exchange exposes one (e.g. `BTC` for inverse/coin-margined futures), and otherwise its quote currency (e.g. `USDT` for `ETH/USDT` and `LTC/USDT`, which would then share the same exposure bucket).
+
+```json
+"max_underlying_exposure": 0.5
+```
+
+With the above configuration, at most 50% of total tradable capital may be committed at any one time to open trades that share a given underlying currency. When opening (or increasing) a trade would push the combined exposure to that pair's underlying currency over the configured limit, the resulting stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit, the same way stake amounts are adjusted for other sizing limits (exchange minimums/maximums, available balance, ...). If no room is left at all, the trade is skipped. This applies identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
+This setting is disabled by default (no limit applied).
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
